# Database Schema Reference

## Canonical Source

[backend/docs/database_schema.md](backend/docs/database_schema.md) is the MySQL 8.4.3 DDL dump exported from HeidiSQL. It is the **single source of truth** for the live database structure.

## When to Read It

Before writing or modifying:

- Eloquent models (`$fillable`, `$casts`, relationships)
- Migrations (new tables, columns, indexes, FKs)
- Raw queries / query builder calls
- Seeders / factories
- Filament Resources (form fields, table columns)

Verify against the dump: table name, column name, type, nullability, FK constraint, unique key, index.

## Maintenance Rule

- **Do NOT hand-edit** `database_schema.md`. It must be re-exported from MySQL whenever the schema changes.
- After creating and running a new migration, remind the developer to re-export the dump.
- Treat any discrepancy between migrations and the dump as a bug and flag it immediately.

